module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- validation-rigid.fenel — the validation rigid atom κ (signature-substrate
-- Phase 4+4b, slice 3a; the S0 proof gate's chosen mechanism).
--
-- WHAT A RIGID IS. Validating a prenex rank-1 scheme means checking its body
-- against ONE arbitrary instance: each quantified variable is replaced by a
-- fresh, check-scoped RIGID ATOM of the same kind. The soundness statement is
-- EQUIVARIANCE — every `Just true` derived at a fresh κ must remain valid when
-- κ is replaced by EVERY well-kinded realizable ground type. "κ does not
-- unify" is NOT that theorem, and the two facts the naive battery missed
-- (κ ⟂ κ must be Nothing because κ := ∅ makes ∅ ⟂ ∅ TRUE; ⊤ ⊆ κ must be
-- Nothing because κ := ⊤ makes it HOLD) are exactly where the difference bites.
--
-- WHY A CONSTRUCTOR AND NOT A RESERVED NAME. The withdrawn candidate was a
-- lexically-bound `SeRef` in a reserved handle namespace. It was live-probe
-- disproven: `SeRef` membership unconditionally enters named-set dispatch and
-- the PUBLIC `registerNamedSet` accepts arbitrary handles, so a registration
-- under a rigid-looking name flips `checkExpr 42 κ` from Nothing to Just true.
-- Enumerate-and-guard across every registry / resolver / μ / normalizer arm is
-- strictly riskier than a constructor with NO arms. `SeRigid` therefore has no
-- named membership, no catalog resolver, no hierarchy, no μ-binding, and no
-- public codec spelling.
--
-- SLICE-3a POSTURE: INERT. Nothing here is judgment-reachable. No checker
-- instantiates a scheme with rigids in this slice (that is 3b); 3a lands the
-- representation, its exhaustive decider matrix (in the deciders themselves,
-- not here), and this module's PURE projection + digest algebra.
--
-- THE Tt-FACE IS PROHIBITED. Validation rigids are checked on the Se face
-- only. This module deliberately declares NO function over `TraversalType`,
-- names no `Tt*` constructor, and never calls the `subset`/`subsetW`
-- containment entry: the have-side `TtVar` path ends in a `Just false`
-- refutation (containment.fenel's `resolveArm` tail) and `isBottomMu` is
-- binder-name-blind, so a rigid crossing into that face could be refuted for
-- structural reasons that do not survive ground substitution. The static gate
-- pins the absence; the deciders' `⊤ ⊆ κ ⇒ Nothing` arm makes the three
-- `TtRefined`-carried crossings abstain rather than refute.
--
-- NON-ESCAPE is ASYMMETRIC (the exclusion posture drafted for this slice was
-- replaced during its own build — see set-marker.ts + the ledger's rig.escape /
-- rig.provenance / rig.kind rows). `SeRigid` IS in the host `SET_EXPR_TAGS`
-- roster: excluding it made every host boundary reclassify a rigid as "not a
-- SetExpr at all" (the silent-swallow class) and made `isSubset(κ,κ)` throw.
-- Instead: `peelSetExpr` recognizes a rigid ONLY when its `kind` is a
-- well-formed closed Kind (rig.kind); the ingress gateway `setExprToTag`
-- THROWS unless an engine-internal decider seam passes
-- `admitValidationRigid: true` (rig.provenance); and the `$`-key egress
-- marshal `setExprToDollarKey` rejects a rigid at any recognized SetExpr
-- child depth — opaque payloads are copied, not walked (rig.escape).
-- The ONLY projection of a rigid that may leave a validation frame is the
-- `fenel.validation.rigid.v1` digest built below.
--
-- FUNCTION PREFIX: every function here carries the `vrg` family prefix so the
-- phase-4 static gate can prove non-reachability by scanning ONE namespace
-- (the `vlg` ledger precedent from slice 2b).
-- =========================================================================

-- One quantified binder of the effective scheme being instantiated. `name` is
-- the SOURCE spelling (used only to find its occurrences in the projection and
-- NEVER hashed); `ordinal` is its position in the effective scheme's quantifier
-- order — the alpha-normal identity; `kind` is its kind (KType or a fully
-- applied KArrow), carried as Any because the kind vocabulary lives in the
-- signature layer.
@entity
@label "ValidationRigidBinder"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — one quantified binder being replaced by a rigid atom: the source spelling (occurrence-finding only, never hashed), the quantifier-order ordinal (the alpha-normal identity), and the binder's kind."
ValidationRigidBinder = VrgBinder name: String ordinal: Nat kind: Any

-- ---- minting -------------------------------------------------------------

@label "validation-rigid: mint"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — mint one rigid atom κ. `scopeToken` must be scope-unique and opaque (two simultaneously live check scopes must not collide even when their source binders share a spelling); `ordinal` is the binder's quantifier-order position; `kind` is its kind. This is the ONLY constructor site for SeRigid outside a test."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgMint : (scopeToken: String) -> (ordinal: Nat) -> (kind: Any) -> SetExpr
vrgMint scopeToken ordinal kind =
  SeRigid { scopeToken = scopeToken, ordinal = ordinal, kind = kind }

-- ---- recognition ---------------------------------------------------------

@label "validation-rigid: isRigid"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — is this node itself a rigid atom? Shallow."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgIsRigid : (s: SetExpr) -> Boolean
vrgIsRigid s = case s of
  SeRigid {} -> true
  _ -> false

-- The DEEP non-escape predicate: does a rigid occur ANYWHERE in this term? Any
-- published view, evidence payload, cache key, diagnostic, or persisted value
-- must answer false. It descends every SetExpr child position, including the
-- SetPattern children an ordinary substitution pass skips.
@label "validation-rigid: hasRigid"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — does a rigid atom occur anywhere in this SetExpr? The deep non-escape predicate: every published view, evidence payload, cache key, diagnostic, and persisted value must answer false. Descends SeCtor fields, SeMu bodies, SeArrow params/returns, boolean branches, AND SetPattern children (SpMatch predicates and SpGroup types)."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "non-escape" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgHasRigid : (s: SetExpr) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigid s = case s of
  SeRigid {} -> true
  SeCtor { fields = fs } -> vrgHasRigidFields fs
  SeMu { body = b } -> vrgHasRigid b
  SeArrow { params = ps, returns = r } ->
    if vrgHasRigidParams ps then true else vrgHasRigid r
  SeUnion { branches = bs } -> vrgHasRigidList bs
  SeIntersect { branches = bs } -> vrgHasRigidList bs
  SeDiff { left = l, right = r } -> if vrgHasRigid l then true else vrgHasRigid r
  SeComplement { inner = i } -> vrgHasRigid i
  SePattern { pattern = p } -> vrgHasRigidPattern p
  _ -> false

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidList"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid over a branch list (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidList : (bs: List SetExpr) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidList bs = case head bs of
  Nothing -> false
  Just b -> if vrgHasRigid b then true else vrgHasRigidList (eufRest bs)

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidFields"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid over SeCtor fields (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidFields : (fs: List SetCtorField) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidFields fs = case head fs of
  Nothing -> false
  Just f -> if vrgHasRigid f.set then true else vrgHasRigidFields (eufRest fs)

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidParams"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid over SeArrow params (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidParams : (ps: List SetArrowParam) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidParams ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> false
  Just p -> if vrgHasRigid p.set then true else vrgHasRigidParams (eufRest ps)

-- DUAL-READ, and the reason is load-bearing. The registered `SetPattern` ADT
-- (SpMatch / SpSeq / …) exists, but NO LIVE DATA USES IT: the runtime carrier
-- nested under `SePattern.pattern` is still the LEGACY `.t`-discriminated host
-- `Pattern` (`{t: "empty"|"eps"|"match"|"seq"|"alt"|"rep"|"group"}`), exactly as
-- `regex-hint.fenel`'s `rxhReadPat` documents and reads it. A `case p of
-- SpMatch {…}` cascade alone therefore falls through to its default on every
-- real value — which would make this non-escape predicate silently blind to a
-- rigid nested under a pattern predicate. So the `Sp*` arms come first (for the
-- eventual data migration) and the `.t` cascade is the live path.
@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidPattern"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid through a pattern's SetExpr children (match predicates, group types). DUAL-READS the registered Sp* ADT and the legacy `.t`-discriminated host Pattern that is the actual runtime carrier — an Sp*-only match would be blind to every live value. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidPattern : (p: a) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidPattern p = case p of
  SpMatch { pred = pr } -> vrgHasRigid pr
  SpSeq { a = x, b = y } -> if vrgHasRigidPattern x then true else vrgHasRigidPattern y
  SpAlt { a = x, b = y } -> if vrgHasRigidPattern x then true else vrgHasRigidPattern y
  SpRep { child = c } -> vrgHasRigidPattern c
  SpGroup { child = c, type = t } ->
    if vrgHasRigidPattern c
    then true
    else case t of
      Just ts -> vrgHasRigid ts
      Nothing -> false
  _ -> vrgHasRigidLegacyPattern p

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidLegacyPattern"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid through the LEGACY `.t`-discriminated host Pattern (the live runtime carrier of SePattern.pattern): match ⇒ pred, seq/alt ⇒ a and b, rep ⇒ child, group ⇒ child plus the optional type slot (read via lookup, since the host form OMITS an absent type rather than carrying Nothing). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidLegacyPattern : (p: a) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidLegacyPattern p =
  case lookup p "t" of
    Nothing -> false
    Just tag ->
      if eq tag "match"
      then vrgHasRigidSlot p "pred"
      else if eq tag "seq"
      then vrgHasRigidPatternSlot p "a" (vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly p "b")
      else if eq tag "alt"
      then vrgHasRigidPatternSlot p "a" (vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly p "b")
      else if eq tag "rep"
      then vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly p "child"
      else if eq tag "group"
      then vrgHasRigidPatternSlot p "child" (vrgHasRigidSlot p "type")
      else false

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigid on an optional SetExpr-valued record slot (absent ⇒ false). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidSlot : (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidSlot p slot = case lookup p slot of
  Nothing -> false
  Just child -> vrgHasRigid child

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidPatternSlotOnly"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigidPattern on an optional pattern-valued record slot (absent ⇒ false). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly : (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly p slot = case lookup p slot of
  Nothing -> false
  Just child -> vrgHasRigidPattern child

@label "validation-rigid: hasRigidPatternSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgHasRigidPattern on a pattern-valued slot, short-circuiting to an already-computed sibling result. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgHasRigidPatternSlot : (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> (orElse: Boolean) -> Boolean
vrgHasRigidPatternSlot p slot orElse =
  if vrgHasRigidPatternSlotOnly p slot then true else orElse

-- ---- the projection rewrite (3a-D2, normative shape) ---------------------

-- D3 projects an instantiated scheme with its quantified variables BOUND, so
-- each occurrence lands as `SeRef {handle = <source spelling>}`, and then runs
-- THIS pure rewrite before ANY decider consultation. Leaving a bound SeRef in
-- place is precisely the withdrawn design — it is capturable through the public
-- `registerNamedSet` — so the rewrite must be TOTAL, and `vrgProject` refuses
-- rather than hand a partially-rigidified term to a decider.
--
-- SHADOWING is honored: a `SeMu {var = a}` rebinds the spelling `a`, so an
-- occurrence inside that body belongs to the fixpoint, not to the scheme's
-- quantifier. Rewriting it would conflate a recursion variable with a rigid.

@label "validation-rigid: nameIn"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — is a spelling present in the shadowed-binder list? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgNameIn : (names: List String) -> (h: String) -> Boolean
vrgNameIn names h = case head names of
  Nothing -> false
  Just n -> if eq n h then true else vrgNameIn (eufRest names) h

@label "validation-rigid: binderFor"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the quantified binder whose source spelling is this handle, if any. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgBinderFor : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (h: String) -> Maybe ValidationRigidBinder
vrgBinderFor bs h = case head bs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> if eq b.name h then Just b else vrgBinderFor (eufRest bs) h

@label "validation-rigid: rigidify"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the PURE projection rewrite: replace every FREE occurrence of a quantified binder's spelling (a bound-projection SeRef) with the rigid atom for that binder. Shadow-aware — a SeMu that rebinds the spelling stops the rewrite inside its body, so a recursion variable is never conflated with a rigid. Total over every SetExpr child position INCLUDING SetPattern children. Pure: no decider is consulted, no registry is read."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "projection" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgRigidify : (scopeToken: String) -> (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (s: SetExpr) -> SetExpr
vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed s = case s of
  SeRef { handle = h } ->
    if vrgNameIn shadowed h
    then s
    else case vrgBinderFor bs h of
      Just b -> vrgMint scopeToken b.ordinal b.kind
      Nothing -> s
  SeCtor { ctor = c, fields = fs } ->
    SeCtor { ctor = c, fields = map (\f -> vrgRigidifyField scopeToken bs shadowed f) fs }
  SeMu { var = v, body = b } ->
    SeMu { var = v, body = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs (appendItem v shadowed) b }
  SeArrow { params = ps, returns = r } ->
    SeArrow
      { params = map (\p -> vrgRigidifyParam scopeToken bs shadowed p) ps
      , returns = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed r
      }
  SeUnion { branches = brs } ->
    SeUnion { branches = map (\x -> vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed x) brs }
  SeIntersect { branches = brs } ->
    SeIntersect { branches = map (\x -> vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed x) brs }
  SeDiff { left = l, right = r } ->
    SeDiff
      { left = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed l
      , right = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed r
      }
  SeComplement { inner = i } ->
    SeComplement { inner = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed i }
  -- SePattern is DELIBERATELY NOT REWRITTEN — it FENCES instead. The runtime
  -- carrier under `SePattern.pattern` is the legacy `.t`-discriminated host
  -- `Pattern`, whose faithful reconstruction in Fenel would have to preserve
  -- `min`/`max` and the OMITTED-vs-Nothing distinction on an optional `type`
  -- slot; a subtly wrong rebuild silently corrupts a pattern, which is worse
  -- than declining. `vrgResidual` dual-reads patterns and reports any surviving
  -- binder spelling, so `vrgProject` returns Nothing for such a term rather
  -- than handing a partially-rigidified projection to a decider. Over-fencing
  -- costs coverage on a corner (a quantified variable inside a regex predicate);
  -- rewriting it wrong would cost correctness.
  _ -> s

@label "validation-rigid: rigidifyField"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgRigidify through one SeCtor field, preserving its identity key and wire projection. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgRigidifyField : (scopeToken: String) -> (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (f: SetCtorField) -> SetCtorField
vrgRigidifyField scopeToken bs shadowed f =
  SetCtorField
    { key = f.key
    , wireName = f.wireName
    , set = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed f.set
    }

@label "validation-rigid: rigidifyParam"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgRigidify through one SeArrow param, preserving its identity key, wire projection, and list position (arity and variance pair strictly by position). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgRigidifyParam : (scopeToken: String) -> (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: SetArrowParam) -> SetArrowParam
vrgRigidifyParam scopeToken bs shadowed p =
  SetArrowParam
    { key = p.key
    , wireName = p.wireName
    , set = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs shadowed p.set
    }

-- ---- the totality post-condition + the public projection entry -----------

@label "validation-rigid: residual"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — does any quantified binder's spelling SURVIVE as a free SeRef after the rewrite? A surviving handle is exactly the withdrawn bound-SeRef design (capturable through the public registerNamedSet), so a true answer must fence the projection rather than reach a decider. Shadow-aware."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "projection" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgResidual : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (s: SetExpr) -> Boolean
vrgResidual bs shadowed s = case s of
  SeRef { handle = h } ->
    if vrgNameIn shadowed h
    then false
    else case vrgBinderFor bs h of
      Just _ -> true
      Nothing -> false
  SeCtor { fields = fs } -> vrgResidualFields bs shadowed fs
  SeMu { var = v, body = b } -> vrgResidual bs (appendItem v shadowed) b
  SeArrow { params = ps, returns = r } ->
    if vrgResidualParams bs shadowed ps then true else vrgResidual bs shadowed r
  SeUnion { branches = brs } -> vrgResidualList bs shadowed brs
  SeIntersect { branches = brs } -> vrgResidualList bs shadowed brs
  SeDiff { left = l, right = r } ->
    if vrgResidual bs shadowed l then true else vrgResidual bs shadowed r
  SeComplement { inner = i } -> vrgResidual bs shadowed i
  SePattern { pattern = p } -> vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed p
  _ -> false

@label "validation-rigid: residualList"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual over a branch list (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualList : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (brs: List SetExpr) -> Boolean
vrgResidualList bs shadowed brs = case head brs of
  Nothing -> false
  Just x ->
    if vrgResidual bs shadowed x then true else vrgResidualList bs shadowed (eufRest brs)

@label "validation-rigid: residualFields"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual over SeCtor fields (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualFields : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (fs: List SetCtorField) -> Boolean
vrgResidualFields bs shadowed fs = case head fs of
  Nothing -> false
  Just f ->
    if vrgResidual bs shadowed f.set then true else vrgResidualFields bs shadowed (eufRest fs)

@label "validation-rigid: residualParams"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual over SeArrow params (any). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualParams : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (ps: List SetArrowParam) -> Boolean
vrgResidualParams bs shadowed ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> false
  Just p ->
    if vrgResidual bs shadowed p.set then true else vrgResidualParams bs shadowed (eufRest ps)

-- DUAL-READ for the same reason vrgHasRigidPattern does: the live carrier is the
-- legacy `.t` host Pattern, so an Sp*-only cascade would report "no residual"
-- for every real pattern and let a partially-rigidified projection through.
@label "validation-rigid: residualPattern"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual through a pattern's SetExpr children. DUAL-READS the registered Sp* ADT and the legacy `.t`-discriminated host Pattern that is the live carrier. Since vrgRigidify deliberately does not rewrite patterns, a binder occurrence found here is what makes vrgProject fence. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualPattern : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: a) -> Boolean
vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed p = case p of
  SpMatch { pred = pr } -> vrgResidual bs shadowed pr
  SpSeq { a = x, b = y } ->
    if vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed x then true else vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed y
  SpAlt { a = x, b = y } ->
    if vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed x then true else vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed y
  SpRep { child = c } -> vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed c
  SpGroup { child = c, type = t } ->
    if vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed c
    then true
    else case t of
      Just ts -> vrgResidual bs shadowed ts
      Nothing -> false
  _ -> vrgResidualLegacyPattern bs shadowed p

@label "validation-rigid: residualLegacyPattern"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual through the LEGACY `.t`-discriminated host Pattern (the live carrier): match ⇒ pred, seq/alt ⇒ a and b, rep ⇒ child, group ⇒ child plus the optional type slot. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualLegacyPattern : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: a) -> Boolean
vrgResidualLegacyPattern bs shadowed p =
  case lookup p "t" of
    Nothing -> false
    Just tag ->
      if eq tag "match"
      then vrgResidualSlot bs shadowed p "pred"
      else if eq tag "seq"
      then vrgResidualPatSlot bs shadowed p "a" (vrgResidualPatSlotOnly bs shadowed p "b")
      else if eq tag "alt"
      then vrgResidualPatSlot bs shadowed p "a" (vrgResidualPatSlotOnly bs shadowed p "b")
      else if eq tag "rep"
      then vrgResidualPatSlotOnly bs shadowed p "child"
      else if eq tag "group"
      then vrgResidualPatSlot bs shadowed p "child" (vrgResidualSlot bs shadowed p "type")
      else false

@label "validation-rigid: residualSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidual on an optional SetExpr-valued record slot (absent ⇒ false). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualSlot : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> Boolean
vrgResidualSlot bs shadowed p slot = case lookup p slot of
  Nothing -> false
  Just child -> vrgResidual bs shadowed child

@label "validation-rigid: residualPatSlotOnly"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidualPattern on an optional pattern-valued record slot (absent ⇒ false). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualPatSlotOnly : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> Boolean
vrgResidualPatSlotOnly bs shadowed p slot = case lookup p slot of
  Nothing -> false
  Just child -> vrgResidualPattern bs shadowed child

@label "validation-rigid: residualPatSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — vrgResidualPattern on a pattern-valued slot, short-circuiting to an already-computed sibling result. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgResidualPatSlot : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (shadowed: List String) -> (p: a) -> (slot: String) -> (orElse: Boolean) -> Boolean
vrgResidualPatSlot bs shadowed p slot orElse =
  if vrgResidualPatSlotOnly bs shadowed p slot then true else orElse

@label "validation-rigid: project"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the PUBLIC projection entry: rigidify the bound-placeholder projection, then verify the rewrite was TOTAL. Just <term> only when no quantified binder spelling survives as a free SeRef; Nothing otherwise (fail closed — a partially-rigidified term must never reach a decider, because a surviving handle is capturable through the public registerNamedSet). Returns a Se-face SetExpr and nothing else: rigids are prohibited from the raw Tt-face containment API."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "projection" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgProject : (scopeToken: String) -> (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (s: SetExpr) -> Maybe SetExpr
vrgProject scopeToken bs s =
  let rewritten = vrgRigidify scopeToken bs [] s
  if vrgResidual bs [] rewritten then Nothing else Just rewritten

-- ---- the canonical rigid digest (3a-D4) ----------------------------------

-- `fenel.validation.rigid.v1` — the ONLY projection of a rigid that leaves a
-- validation frame. Runtime rigid tokens are opaque and scope-unique; they
-- never supply their nonce OR their source spelling to canonical bytes. The
-- alpha-normal identity is the quantifier-order ORDINAL, carried as a number.
--
-- ORDINAL-AS-NUMBER, deliberately. The brief's alpha-normal names are `r0, r1,
-- …`; rendering the ordinal to that string would put a host number through
-- `toString`, and a cloned decider context BOXES numbers there (the recorded
-- `[object Object]` landmine). The ordinal itself is the same normalization
-- with no rendering step, and the S2 encoder writes it as big-endian binary64.
-- The entry carries its own ordinal, so a caller that passes binders out of
-- quantifier order produces a DIFFERENT digest (detectable) rather than a
-- silent collision with the correctly-ordered one.
--
-- The scope record is the semantic scope {validatorVersion, sccId, functionId,
-- schemeHash}: repeat validation of identical semantic input must produce the
-- same digest, while two live check scopes stay non-unifiable at the ATOM level
-- through their distinct scopeTokens (which is a SetExpr fact, not a hash fact).
--
-- The S2 canonical-byte encoder + SHA-256 leaf consume this payload; slice 3a
-- deliberately leaves that wiring to the slice-3b validator, so the encoder
-- keeps its production-unconsumed posture for one more slice.

@label "validation-rigid: digestRigids"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the alpha-normalized rigid entries for the fenel.validation.rigid.v1 payload: ordinal (the quantifier-order alpha-normal identity) plus kind, in caller-supplied quantifier order. The source spelling and the runtime scopeToken are deliberately absent. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "rigid" "digest" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vrgDigestRigids : (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> (acc: List Any) -> List Any
vrgDigestRigids bs acc = case head bs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just b -> vrgDigestRigids (eufRest bs) (appendItem { ordinal = b.ordinal, kind = b.kind } acc)

@label "validation-rigid: digestPayload"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3a — the fenel.validation.rigid.v1 canonical-byte payload: the domain literal, the alpha-normalized rigid entries (ordinal + kind only — never a scopeToken, never a source spelling), and the semantic scope {validatorVersion, sccId, functionId, schemeHash}. Identical semantic input yields identical bytes; the S2 encoder + SHA-256 leaf turn it into the domain-tagged digest that is the ONLY rigid projection allowed out of a validation frame."
@tags "engine" "validation" "rigid" "digest" "non-escape" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vrgDigestPayload : (validatorVersion: String) -> (sccId: String) -> (functionId: String) -> (schemeHash: String) -> (bs: List ValidationRigidBinder) -> Any
vrgDigestPayload validatorVersion sccId functionId schemeHash bs =
  { domain = "fenel.validation.rigid.v1"
  , rigids = vrgDigestRigids bs []
  , scope =
      { validatorVersion = validatorVersion
      , sccId = sccId
      , functionId = functionId
      , schemeHash = schemeHash
      }
  }
